why: How a colab is packed and how a return is read. Not a run. Not live.

cite: 8.9

## Pack
Why: because a cold model that is given the whole book answers from the average.

Body: Pack only the pages the job needs. Door first. Then the seat under test. A fixture if the job is a repair. Not the whole book. Not a retired `.09`. Not the sleeve's memory. ~~Ship it as a zip in `zips/outbound`, outside the kernel.~~ The ship path is page 0037 pack.

## Door
Why: because a cold model does not remember the walk.

Body: Open `00.start`, then the named book door, then the axioms. `00.readme` is the map if the sleeve is unsure.

## Job
Why: because two jobs in one pack is how a return cannot be graded.

Body: One sentence. What the cold model is to do.

## Ask
Why: because a nod is not a break.

Body: The return shape. Scores first. Opinion second. Tests are attacks. They are not a score the sleeve is asked to beat.

## Hostile
Why: because a sleeve that is not given a path will obey the draft as live.

Body: Name the path that should break. Name the face you were tempted to obey as live. Include the tests. Gravity around five. Fewer or more is discretion. A repair may take four. A factfind may take seven. Returns link to the actual page.

## Check
Why: because a named file left out of the zip is our halt, not a hole in the drawing.

Body: Before the zip, walk every page the fixture names, every cite, and the door. If a page is missing, ship it, or write on the door that the sleeve takes it on that page's word. A file withheld on purpose must say so, and why. A halt on a named withhold is not a finding. A halt on a file that is neither included nor withheld is a pack fail. Discard that halt. Do not call it a factfind.

## Factfind
Why: because the holes are the work, and an opinion has to have a fence.

Body: Holes the pack does not finish. Point at the page. Number them, so pass `02` can say hole `1` closed or hole `1` still open. An opinion on how to solve is allowed here, and only here.

## Overflow
Why: because what did not fit will be invented later if it is not parked.

Body: What did not fit. Park it.

## Unprompted
Why: because the sleeve that only answers the ask hides the miss.

Body: One thing you would have written differently, and why.

## Return
Why: because a return that is not a file is lost.

Body: One file per page, plus one factfind. Chain, break, repair. Short. The difference only. The filename is `(modelname)-(colabname)-(passNN)-(date)`. ~~It lands in `returns`, on the root, outside the kernel.~~ The return path is page 0038 return. A return is not a promote.

patch: 2026-10-10. report #14. >point. Colab explains. The ship path is page 0037 pack. The return path is page 0038 return.
The prime reads it in two passes. First read and note. Then make the `# NN` jobs. Do not write a seat in either pass.

## Pieces
Why: because one pass across the book cannot be reviewed, and the last one made a hole.

Body: The jobs split into three. Gravity is 5.
1. Decisions. What must change, before any write.
2. Drafts, patches, fixes, strikes. Only what the decisions named.
3. Park. Named, not done.

## Temp
Why: because a return written straight onto a seat will eat the page.

Body: The notes and the jobs are written on one temp page first. A seat is not opened for a write until that page has been read. A pass that overwrites a seat is a halt.

## Prime
Why: because the sleeve that wrote the pack must not grade only its own sentences.

Body: The prime job on a returned colab is the report. Read one page, then one face. Notes on face `06`. A hole that needs work becomes a `05.NN`. Batch as `#NN` so each finding can be released or held. Do not patch the live face from the return.

The report has five parts.
Overview: the scope of the result.
Learned: what the return taught.
Issue: omit unless the sleeves conflict. Give the options, and the suggestion.
Why: the reason for the choice.
Ask: the `>` you want, so the director can release it.

